# Chapter 11, part 1: the message line and the boxes of the Editor.
.h2 The Editor: the message line [msg-editor-line]
.ix Message line, Editor
.ix Messages, Editor, message line
.ix Editor, messages
The Editor puts these lines on the message line.  A line stays until the next
key.  None of them prompts for a key; the ones that reject something leave the
document as it was.  The line is described in {x:view-message}.
.h3 Refusals and information [msg-editor-line-refusals]
.table 26 34
Message | Meaning and what to do
A Print Error cannot be made by hand | A Print Error marker was chosen in the
 | Marker command.  Only a print makes that marker; the document was not
 | changed.
Adjust needs two windows that share the screen | Edit, Window, Adjust: one window is open, or a window fills the screen.
Autosort sorts blocks | Sort was asked for something that is not a block
 | selection.  Choose Autosort again and highlight blocks.
Block selection must stay within one section | The highlight of Cut, Copy,
 | Delete, Move or Autosort includes a section tag or a heading.  Highlight
 | blocks of one section only, or use the section selection of the command.
Border: N changes | Border applied the settings of the panel to the highlighted
 | columns and blocks.
Cancelled | {k:Esc} ended a highlight: the command did nothing.
Cannot calculate: the expression is not good | Math found an operator with
 | nothing to work on, an exponent that is not a whole number, a number of more
 | than 100 digits or one that is too large.  Change the numbers.
Cannot delete the only block | Delete Block on the only block of a section
 | that cannot be removed with it (an unstructured document, or a section that
 | has subsections).  Delete the section, or put other text in the block.
Cannot delete the only section | Delete Section when the document has a single
 | section. A structured document always keeps one.
Cannot divide by zero | Math was asked to divide by zero.  The clipboard is not
 | changed.
Cannot join a section that has subsections | Join Section on a section that is
 | followed by subsections.  Join the subsections first, or move them.
Cannot join here | Join found nothing to join and had no more exact message.
 | Move the cursor to another place and try again.
Cannot take the whole document as a section | A section highlight that starts
 | at the first section (the root).  Highlight a part of the document.
Capitalized: N characters changed | Case, Capitalize.  {c:1 character} for
 | one.  Upper case: and Lower case: are the same for those choices.
Collapse/expand works in structured documents | Expand, Contract or a fold key
 | in an unstructured document.  There are no sections to fold.
Copied | Copy finished.  The area is in the clipboard.
Cut | Cut finished.  The area is in the clipboard.
Deleted | Delete finished.  Unlike Cut, Delete does not put the area in the
 | clipboard.
Equation drawn as Short: REASON | The cursor is on an Equation, shown with the
 | display mode Inline, whose picture cannot be made.  The marker is drawn in
 | its Short form, {c:[EQN text]}.  REASON is the first line of the message
 | ({n:eq-messages}); the Error Log of the run has the place of the marker.
Found | Search found the text and the cursor is on it.
Hanging indent set at {i:N} | {k:Ctrl-H} made a hanging indent whose second
 | and later lines begin at position N.
Highlight text, Enter to cut | {k:Ctrl-X} began a highlight of text.  Move the
 | cursor, then {k:Enter}; {k:Esc} cancels.
Highlight the area with the cursor keys, then press Enter (Esc cancels) | Move
 | (F7) began a highlight.  Move the cursor, then {k:Enter}.
Highlighting: move the cursor, Enter to accept, Esc to cancel | A highlight of
 | Cut, Copy or Delete is on.  Same keys.
Ins saves, Esc restores, Ctrl-W views the equation | The editing window of an
 | equation (Marker, Alt-F12 on an equation) is open. {k:Ins} keeps the
 | changes, {k:Esc} gives the old text back, {k:Ctrl-W} shows the equation
 | ({n:eq-view}).
Join works on single-column blocks | Join Block on a block that has more than
 | one column.  Join the columns first (Join Column), or use Split.
Keycap drawn as Short: REASON | The same for a Keycap, drawn as
 | {c:[Key: legend]}.
LaTeX marker drawn as Short: REASON | The cursor is on a LaTeX marker, shown
 | with the display mode Inline, that is not drawn as a picture.  REASON is a
 | phrase that says why: a marker that begins or ends a block, a list, a table
 | or a conditional, a definition, a counter or a setting that the text after
 | it uses, a command that is not safe to run, or a text that is too long or
 | damaged ({n:markers}).  The first line of a message of LaTeX is the reason
 | when the text did not typeset.
Leave Section edit before moving blocks or sections | Move: Section edit is on, and a block or a section cannot move then.  Leave it with {k:Ctrl-^}.
Left, Right, Home and End move columns | Move Column: another key was pressed.
Marker type {i:N} cannot be edited | The cursor is on a marker whose type is
 | not in the table of Strata; N is its number.  Delete it or leave it.
Moved | Move: {k:Enter} kept the columns, blocks or sections where they are.
Moving: the cursor keys move it, Enter accepts, Esc cancels | Move: a key that is not a cursor key was pressed while the area moves.
No following peer section | Join Section on the last section of its level.
No letter was changed | Case: the text that was highlighted had no letter to
 | change (or all of them were in that case).
No previous peer section | Demote ({k:Alt-]}) found that the section before
 | has another level.  Move the section first.
No previous section to become a subsection of | Demote on the first section.
No section here | Append Section or Append Subsection found that the cursor is
 | outside every section.  Move into a section.
No section {i:NAME} | Go To Section: the number NAME is not in the document.
 | Use Go To again and type a number such as 2.1.
No word under the cursor | Case with nothing highlighted: the cursor is not at
 | a word.
Not found: {i:TEXT} | Search or Replace did not find TEXT. TEXT is the string, or
 | what was looked for ({c:a tab}, {c:an end of line}, {c:a no-break space},
 | {c:a marker}, or {c:bold text} for an attribute with no string).  The cursor
 | does not move.
Nothing is highlighted: highlight the numbers to calculate | Math was chosen with
 | no highlight.  Highlight the numbers and choose Math again.
Nothing to join here | The Delete key, at the end of the last column of a
 | block, would join the next block and found none.  There is nothing to do.
Nothing to paste | Paste ({k:F5}) when the clipboard is empty.  Cut or copy
 | first.
Nothing to redo | Redo ({k:Alt-/}) when no operation has been undone, or a
 | new change took the undone operations away.
Nothing to sort | The section has fewer than two subsections.
Nothing to undo | Undo ({k:Ctrl-/}) when nothing has been changed since the
 | document was loaded, or the operations were all taken back.
Only a structured document has sections | Edit, Section ({k:Ctrl-^}) in an
 | unstructured document.
Overtype off | Overtype is off. ({k:Alt-F5} and {k:Ins} switch it.)
Overtype on | Overtype is on.  Typed letters replace the letters at the cursor.
Picture drawn as Short: REASON | The same for a Picture whose file cannot be
 | made into a picture.
Press Ins to Save Changes or Esc to Restore Previous Version | The editing
 | window of a note or footnote, or of another text of a marker, is open.  Same
 | keys.
Section selection must cover peer sections | The highlight of a section
 | command begins and ends in different levels or cuts a section in half.
 | Highlight whole sections of one level.
Sections exist only in structured documents | Sort Sections, or a section
 | highlight, in an unstructured document.
Sort direction: ascending | While the highlight of Autosort is on, the key
 | {k:+} or {k:-} was typed.  Ascending is the default; each of the keys
 | switches the direction.
Sort direction: descending | Same, descending.
Sorted {i:N} blocks | Autosort ordered N blocks.
Sorted {i:N} sections | Sort Sections ordered N subsections.
Split a block of several columns by column | Split Block on a block that has
 | more than one column.  Split by column instead.
Text selection must stay within one column | A text highlight that crosses
 | from one column to another.  Highlight inside one column.
The block cannot move farther | Move Block: the block is at the first or the last place of its section.
The block has one column only | Move Column: a block with one column has nothing to move to.
The column cannot move farther | Move Column: the column is the first or the last one.
The cursor is not in a block | Spell Check Block or Section, Autosort or
 | Preview Block when the cursor is on a section tag or a heading.  Move into
 | the text of a block.
The file has no named block settings | Retrieve, with the option Retrieve Named Block Settings Only: the file has no named block format.
The headline of a section cannot move | Move Block: the headline is the first block of its section and stays there.
The section cannot move | Move Section: the section is not inside another section.
The section cannot move farther | Move Section: the section is at the place where the key would take it (the first or the last, or the next level would not exist).
The section cannot move left | Promote ({k:Alt-[}) on a section of the first
 | level.  Nothing is above it.
The section has no subsections to sort | Sort Sections on a section that has
 | none.
There is no block to put a border on | Border found no block in the highlight.
 | Highlight a column of a block.
There is no column to put a border on | The highlight of Border does not cover
 | a column of the block.  Highlight at least one column and choose Border
 | again.
There is no current section | Edit, Section ({k:Ctrl-^}) or Sort Sections when
 | the cursor is outside every section.
There is no number to calculate | The highlight that Math was given holds no
 | number.  Highlight text that has the numbers and the operators.
There is one window only | Edit, Window, Close or Switch: only one window is open.
Two windows are open already | Edit, Window, Open: a second window is open.
Type the hanging characters first, then press Ctrl-H | {k:Ctrl-H} at the first
 | position of a line: the hanging indent is measured to the position of the
 | cursor, so there is nothing to measure.  Type the bullet or number, then
 | press the key.
Up and Down change the size of the windows; Enter accepts, Esc cancels | Edit, Window, Adjust: the keys that change the size.
Up, Down, Home and End move blocks | Move Block: another key was pressed.
Use arrow keys to highlight block(s); then press Enter. | Spell Check Block or
 | Preview: highlight blocks and press {k:Enter}.  The line for Section says
 | {c:section(s)}.
Use arrow keys to highlight block(s); then press Enter.  Home, End: begin or
 end of section. +, -: change direction | Autosort Table began a highlight.
 | {k:Home} and {k:End} go to the ends of the section, {k:+} and {k:-} set the
 | direction of the sort.
Use arrow keys to highlight column(s); then press Enter | {k:Alt-F8}, Border began a
 | highlight of columns.  Move the cursor to cover the columns and press
 | {k:Enter}; the panel of the border opens.
Window closed | Edit, Window, Close closed the window of the cursor.
Window opened: retrieve or create a document in it | Edit, Window, Open opened a second window.
.end
.h3 After a command has done its work [msg-editor-line-done]
These lines tell what a command did.  Every one of them is also given in the
chapter of the command.
.table 27 33
Message | After
Defining Alt-{i:K}: press Ctrl-F1 to end | Learn: every key is now recorded
 | for the macro Alt-K until {k:Ctrl-F1}.
Deleted | Delete Macro or Delete from Library: the macro or the entry is gone.
Deleted {i:PATH} | Delete (File).
Exported {i:PATH} | Export.
Imported; {i:N} characters not kept | Import with UTF-8 or Latin-1: N characters
 | became question marks (1 character).
Imported {i:PATH} | Import.  See {x:file-messages-line}.
Library entry {i:NAME} made | Copy to Library.  The entry NAME is in the
 | library.
Library not loaded: REASON | The start of the Editor.  The file of the Setup
 | field Initial Library cannot be read or is not a library; the Editor
 | started without it.
Macro Alt-{i:K} has {i:N} keystrokes | The entry of a macro was accepted; K is
 | the key, N the number of keystrokes (1 keystroke).
Macro set not loaded: REASON | The start of the Editor.  The file of the Setup
 | field Initial Macro Set cannot be read or is not a macro set; the Editor
 | started without it.
N library entries | The library has N entries (after Cut to Library or the
 | Library Edit panel was accepted). {c:1 library entry} for one.
N replacements | Replace changed N places. {c:1 replacement} for one;
 | {c:(stopped)} is added when {k:Q} or {k:Esc} ended the run.
New document | New.
{c:No UTF-8 terminal: ASCII is drawn. The font is not checked. See Setup.} | The
 | start of the Editor, and of the Document Manager (on its footer line).  The
 | terminal does not read UTF-8, so the screen is drawn with ASCII characters
 | ({n:appterm-charset}).  The font cannot be checked.  Field Terminal
 | Characters of Setup and the variable STRATA_ASCII change the choice.
Not included in the library | Copy to Library with Include in Library? set to
 | No: nothing was stored.
Preview cancelled | {k:Esc} was pressed while the preview was prepared.
Preview done | The Viewer was closed after a good preview.
Preview done: PRINT FAILED, N print errors (Ctrl-F8 finds the next) | The
 | Viewer was closed after a preview that had errors ({n:print-failed}).
Preview done; the viewer could not show N things: TEXT | The Viewer left
 | something out of the pages (TEXT names the first); the preview is
 | otherwise good.  When the run has a log the line ends with "; details in
 | the log of the run" ({n:appcfg-log}).
Preview: the viewer failed: TEXT | The Viewer ended with an error; TEXT is
 | the reason.  When the run has a log the line ends with "; details in the
 | log of the run" ({n:appcfg-log}).
Replace needs the text to search for | Replace was accepted with Find at Text
 | and no string to search for.  Nothing was changed.
Replace?  R replace  O once  S skip  A all  Q quit | Replace stopped at a place
 | and waits for a key ({n:edit-b-replace}).
Retrieved N library entries | Retrieve Library. {c:1 library entry} for one.
Retrieved N macros | Retrieve Macros. {c:1 macro} for one.
Retrieved {i:PATH} | Retrieve (and the Retrieve of the list at the start).
Saved {i:PATH} | Save, Save Library, Save Macros.
Saved {i:PATH} (no backup made: {i:REASON}) | Save, when the document was
 | saved but its backup could not be made (the directory .backup cannot be made
 | or written, or a file named .backup is in the way).  The document is
 | saved; the reason shows what to mend.
Saved {i:PATH} (no change, no backup made) | Save, when the file on disk
 | holds exactly what Save would write: nothing was written and no backup was
 | made or moved.
.end
.h2 The Editor: boxes [msg-editor-boxes]
.ix Boxes, Editor
.ix Messages, Editor boxes
.ix Press any key, Editor
The boxes of the Editor appear over the text and wait for a key.  Each table
gives the title of the box first (the name of the command or of the area), then
the text, then the meaning.  The panel that was open when the box appeared is
shown again, unless the table says that the command is over.
.h3 File: Save, Retrieve, New, Delete, Import, Export [msg-ed-file]
.ix Messages, File boxes
.ix Save failed
.ix Retrieve failed
.ix Import failed
.ix Export failed
{x:file-messages} describes each of these in the context of its command.
{c:PATH} below is the full name of the file.  Several reasons of the document
reader are in lower case ({c:cannot open file}, {c:read error}): they are the
words of the program, not those of the system, and they do not name which
system error occurred.
.table 22 13 25
Title and text | Command | Meaning and what to do
A backup file is not saved over: use Restore Backup or give another name |
 Save | The name is the name of a backup: the extension {c:.bak} or {c:.bak} and
 | | digits, or a file in the directory {c:.backup}.  Nothing is written.  Save
 | | with another name, or use Restore Backup.
Delete: Cannot delete the file | Delete | The file could not be removed.  It is
 | | a directory, or the directory is protected.  Check the rights.
Delete: Cannot find the file | Delete | The name is not a file of the Working
 | | Directory.  Add the extension.
Export failed: cannot write PATH | Export | The file cannot be created.  The
 | | directory does not exist or is protected.  Give another Working Directory.
Export failed: There is no current section | Export, scope Export Current
 | Section | The cursor is in no section.
Export failed: write error on PATH | Export | The disk is full, or the write
 | | failed at the end.  Free some space.
Import failed: cannot open file | Import | No such file, or no right to
 | | read it.
Import failed: read error | Import | The file was opened and could not be read
 | | through.  Try again, or copy the file.
Import failed: this is a directory, not a file | Import | The name is the name
 | | of a directory.  Type the name of a file.
Open the part that can be read? | Retrieve, Open, the Editor started on a file |
 | | The file is cut short or damaged after a readable beginning. Y opens the
 | | blocks before the damage as the new document NAME.recovered.doc; N and Esc
 | | open nothing.  The file is not changed.
Recovered N blocks of NAME; the original is not changed | Retrieve, Open |
 | | The part of a damaged file is open as a new, unsaved document.
Retrieve failed: cannot open file | Retrieve, New (template) | No such file,
 | | or no right to read it.  Check the name and the Working Directory.
Retrieve failed: damaged document: a piece of text has no end | Retrieve |
 | | The file is damaged: it is cut short.  Use the newest backup (Restore
 | | Backup, if backups are kept).
Retrieve failed: Nothing to apply | Retrieve | A kind of retrieve that has
 | | nothing in the file to take.  Choose Retrieve Entire Document.
Retrieve failed: read error | Retrieve | The file could not be read through.
Retrieve failed: The file is not a document of this software. | Retrieve |
 | | The file is a text file or another kind of file.  Use Import for a text
 | | file.
Retrieve failed: The file is version N.  This software reads up to version 3.
 | Retrieve | The file was written by a newer version of the software.  Use
 | | the newer software, which reads the file.
Retrieve failed: The file version is N.  This software reads versions 2 to 3.
 | Retrieve | The version of the file is below the oldest that is read, or it
 | | is damaged (a damaged version is shown in quotation marks).
Save failed: cannot write file | Save | The directory or the file does not
 | | allow writing.  Give another Working Directory or name.
Save failed: cannot write PATH | Save Global Settings Only, Extract | Same.
Save failed: There is no current section | Extract Current Section | The
 | | cursor is in no section.
Save failed: write error | Save | The disk is full or failed.  The old file is
 | | not touched.
Template: Cannot find the template file | New | The Template field names a
 | | file that is not in the directories of templates
 | | ({n:file-templates-path}).
Template: the text of the reading error | New | The template is not a document
 | | (the reasons of Retrieve above).
.end
.h3 The panels: refused values [msg-ed-panels]
.ix Panel refusals, messages
.ix Marker, title of a panel box
.ix Refusal box
Every panel is checked as a whole when {k:Ins} is pressed.  A wrong value shows
one of the messages below in a box, and the panel stays open with nothing
applied.  The box title is
that of the area, with one exception that the user would not expect: the check
of the panels of the File commands, Print and Preview, the Macros, the
Library and the Marker panels shows its box under the title {c:Marker},
whatever panel refused.  Read the text, not the title.  The panels of Global
Format, Page and Named have their own titles.
.table 23 12 25
Text | Panel | Meaning and what to do
Cannot find section number | Marker (Cross-reference) | The section number is
 | | not in the document.
Counter must be 1 to 99 | Marker (Counter) | The counter number is not a whole
 | | number from 1 to 99.
FIELD must be 0.0 to 100.0 | Marker (Keycap) | The Foreground or the
 | | Background is not from 0.0 to 100.0.  FIELD is the name of the field.
File must be specified (File Name) | Macros: Save | The File Name field is
 | | empty.
No file name specified | All File panels and Library | The name field is
 | | empty.
No string specified | Marker | A text field that must have text is empty.
Not a valid number (LABEL) | Marker | A numeric field has something else than
 | | a number with the right number of decimals. LABEL is the field.
Not a valid revision number | Save, New | Revision is not digits with at most
 | | three decimals.  Type 2 or 1.25.
Scale must be 0.001 to 10.000 | Marker (Keycap) | The Scale is less than 0.001
 | | or more than 10.
Set Value must be 0 to 4294967295 | Marker (Counter) | The Set Value is not a
 | | whole number from 0 to 4294967295.
The macro key is a letter or a digit | Macros | Macro Key: Alt- has no letter
 | | or digit, or has more than one.
.end
The same box title is used for the refusals of the markers
({n:msg-ed-marker}).
.h3 Further reasons for a refused value [msg-ed-reasons]
.ix Reasons for a refused value
.ix Refused values, reasons
These texts are the reasons that the programs give for a value, a file or a
backup that is refused.  They are shown in the box of a refusal, on the
message line or after {c:no backup made:} on the line of a save.
.table 25 12 23
Text | Where | Meaning and what to do
{c:A header or footer has at most three parts, separated by |} | Global, Page |
 The text of a header or a footer has more than three parts: the parts for the
 left, the center and the right are separated by the bar.
A header or footer takes plain ASCII text | Global, Page | A character of the
 text is not ASCII.  Use the markers for special characters.
A word with an equals sign has no hyphen: it is never broken | Maintain Dictionaries |
 The entry has an equals sign: the word is kept whole.  A notice.
cannot make backup 1: REASON; the document that was replaced is the file NAME |
 Save | The old version could not be put into the directory of the backups.
 The document is saved; the old version is the file NAME.
{c:cannot make the folder DIR: REASON} | Save | The directory of the backups
 cannot be made.
cannot move a backup: REASON | Save | A numbered backup could not be renumbered.
cannot move the backups: REASON; the document that was replaced is the file
 NAME | Save | The same, for the whole row of backups.
cannot restore: not a regular file | Restore Backup | The backup is not an
 ordinary file.
cannot write file: not a regular file | Save | The name is a directory or
 another file that is not an ordinary file.
Gutter Size must be a number such as 0.250 | Global, Page | Gutter Size has a
 letter, a sign or more than three decimals.
{c:lpinfo could not be started} | Print | Search for printers could not run {c:lpinfo}.
{c:lpinfo was not found in the system folders}
 {c:(/usr/bin, /usr/sbin and the others): install the cups package} | Print | Search for printers needs {c:lpinfo}
 of the cups package.
Number of Columns must be from 1 to 9 | Global, Page | Number of Columns is
 not a whole number from 1 to 9.
Search for printers only looks for printers: choose File only, PDF viewer or a
 printer to print | Print | Search for printers was started with a value of
 Printer that is not a queue.  Choose one of the three values.
Sides or sort is not a known choice | Print | A value of Sides or Sort is not
 one of the choices.
The description has at most N characters, with no control character | Save,
 New | The Description is too long or has a control character.
The hyphenation dictionary gives N words and has M | Maintain Dictionaries | The count in
 the file is not the number of words.  The file is damaged.
The hyphenation dictionary is damaged | Maintain Dictionaries | The file has an error.
 Choose another or restore the file.
{c:the name of the folder DIR is too long} | Save | The directory of the backups
 would have a name that is too long.  No backup is made.
{c:The name of the output file is longer than 255 bytes} | Print | Output File is
 too long.  Give a shorter name.
The PDF Directory cannot be written | Print | The directory exists and cannot
 be written.  Check the rights.
The PDF Directory does not exist | Print | The directory is not there.  Make
 it, or give another.
The PDF Directory starts with ~/, but the home directory of the user is not
 known | Print | The variable HOME is not set.
{c:The PDF viewer can be changed by other users (its file or its directory
 is writable by others, or it belongs to another user), so it is not started}
 | Print | The viewer is not used, for safety.  Use a program that only its
 owner can change.
The PDF viewer is not an executable file that you can run | Print | The name
 is not a program.
The PDF viewer must be a program that shows PDF files, not a word processor |
 Print | The name is that of a word processor.
The PDF viewer must be given with its full path, such as /usr/bin/evince
 (letters, digits and . _ + - only, no space, no ..) | Print | The name of the
 viewer is not a full path of that form.
the PDF was not given with its full path | Print | The PDF Directory or the
 name of the PDF does not give a full path.
{c:This is not a hyphenation dictionary (its size is not a whole number of
 pages)} | Maintain Dictionaries | The file chosen is not a dictionary of hyphenation.
.end
.h3 Global: Format, Page, Options, Named [msg-ed-global]
.ix Messages, Global
.ix Messages, Options
.ix Options, could not be saved
These are described with their panels in {x:format-messages}; the table lists
them for the lookup.
.table 22 15 23
Text | Title | Meaning and what to do
Enter a name to save the format as | Named Block Format | Save as is empty.
FIELD must be 0 to 100 | Page Layout | Vertical Centering is not a whole
 | | number from 0 to 100.
FIELD must be a number such as 1.000 | Page Layout | A margin, an indent or a
 | | whitespace is not a number with at most three decimals.
FIELD must be a number such as 1.50 | Format | A spacing is not a number.
FIELD must be a whole number | Format | A field of whole numbers has a sign, a
 | | point or a letter.
Foreground and Background are 0.0 to 100.0, Scale is 0.100 to 10.000 | Keycap
 | Format (box titled Marker) | A value of the keycap panel is out of range.
Invalid number | Named Block Format | A name with a control character, a
 | | spacing with more than two decimals, or a whole number field with a
 | | letter.
There are no named block formats | Delete Named Block | The document has none.
.end
When Options is accepted the settings are written to the file of the user.  If
that fails, a box titled Options shows one of the messages of
{x:appcfg-write-errors} ({c:There is no home directory}, {c:Cannot make DIR:
REASON}, {c:DIR is not a directory of yours}, {c:Cannot write FILE: REASON}).
The settings stay valid until the Editor ends.
.h3 Marker and the commands that make markers [msg-ed-marker]
.ix Messages, markers
.ix Invalid marker selection
.table 27 33
Text | Meaning and what to do
Invalid marker selection (Not available in an unstructured document) | Box
 | titled Marker.  The marker chosen (a section marker such as a
 | cross-reference to a section tag) needs a structured document.  Choose
 | another or make the document structured.
Invalid marker selection (Not available in document body) | Box titled Marker.
 | The marker belongs only to headers, footers or the title page, not to the
 | body of the text.
Marker type N cannot be edited | Message line: see the table of the message
 | line.
.end
The panels of a marker are checked with the messages of {x:msg-ed-panels}.
{n:markers} gives the panel of each marker.
.h3 Tools: Macros and Library [msg-ed-tools]
.ix Messages, Macros
.ix Messages, Library
.ix Library messages
.ix Macro messages
.table 20 13 27
Text | Title | Meaning and what to do
Enter a name for the entry | Copy to Library | Entry name is empty.
Enter the name of the entry | Library Entry | Entry Name is empty.
No such library entry | Delete from Library, Paste from Library | The name is
 | | not in the library.  Press {k:F2} in the field to see them.
No such macro | Delete Macro | The key has no macro.
That file is not a library | Retrieve failed | The file loaded, but is not
 | | a library.  It is a document or a macro set.
That file is not a macro set | Retrieve failed | Same for a macro file.
The keystrokes are not understood (a key name is in < >, and < is <<) | Macro
 | Edit | The text of Keystrokes has a key name that is not known, or an
 | | unbalanced angle bracket.  Write {c:<Enter>} for Enter and {c:<<} for the
 | | sign.
The library has no entries | Delete from Library, Paste from Library
 | | Retrieve or make an entry first.
There are no macros | Delete Macro | Make a macro first.
.end
The reading errors of Retrieve Macros and Retrieve Library are the texts of
{x:msg-ed-file} (the box is titled Retrieve failed) except that the refusal of a file that is not a
library or not a macro set is one of the texts in the table above.
.table 20 13 27
Text | Title | Meaning and what to do
cannot open file | Retrieve failed | A macro file that cannot be opened.  The
 | | other reasons of the reader are in {x:msg-ed-file}.
Cannot write the file | Save failed | A macro file that cannot be written
 | | (Save Macro Set).
.end
.h3 Print and Preview [msg-ed-print]
.ix Messages, Print panel
.ix Messages, Preview panel
The values of the Print and Preview panels are checked when
{k:Ins} is pressed; the messages of the checks and of the run are in
{x:msg-job}.  The two boxes below are for the panel only.
.table 23 12 25
Text | Title | Meaning and what to do
The cursor is not in a block | Preview | Preview Block with the cursor off a
 | | block.
There is no current section | Preview | Preview Section when the cursor is in
 | | no section.
.end
